## Temporal SDK

Generated projects use Temporal Rust SDK 1.1.0 with typed workflows and activities.
Client policies such as `WorkflowIdReusePolicy` come from `temporalio_client`;
workers attach to the active Tokio runtime with `Runtime::from_current_tokio`.
The example uses stable APIs and does not enable the SDK's `experimental` feature.

From the generated project, run the deterministic activity test and the optional
workflow integration test:

```sh
cargo test -p {{project-name}}-core --features temporal-tests temporal::tests::activity_completes
cargo test -p {{project-name}}-core --features temporal-tests temporal::tests::workflow_completes -- --ignored
```

The workflow test downloads and starts an ephemeral Temporal CLI dev server;
it requires network access on the first run but no PostgreSQL instance.
The `temporal-tests` feature enables SDK testing and the downloader's TLS backend.

Migration references: [0.8.0 release notes](https://github.com/temporalio/sdk-rust/releases/tag/v0.8.0),
[1.0.0 release notes](https://github.com/temporalio/sdk-rust/releases/tag/v1.0.0),
and [1.1.0 release notes](https://github.com/temporalio/sdk-rust/releases/tag/v1.1.0).
